description: Prove behavior with tests; do not skip or invent coverage
alwaysApply: true
---

# Verification

Distinguish code that works from code you think works.

- Bug fixes: write a failing reproduction test first, then fix, then watch it pass.
- Run existing tests before and after. If they already failed, say so. Do not let your change take the blame.
- Test behavior, not constructors or trivial getters. Cover the interesting cases (bad input, auth failure, missing file).
- If you cannot write a test, say why (e.g. DB calls coupled to business logic). Do not skip quietly.
